    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Six British colonies federated by popular referendum on 1 January 1901, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-barton">Edmund Barton</a> as first prime minister.</li><li>Its constitution blends Westminster responsible government with an American-style Senate, federalism and a High Court.</li><li>A British dominion became an independent, multicultural nation by gradual steps, ending in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia-act-1986">Australia Act</a> of 1986.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The plan for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canberra">Canberra</a> came from an international competition won in 1912 by the American architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-burley-griffin">Walter Burley Griffin</a>, with drawings by his wife and partner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marion-mahony-griffin">Marion Mahony Griffin</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

